  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contracting in New Hampshire totaled $1.9B in obligations in FY2026 to date. New Hampshire recorded 4,091 awards over the same period, with an average award size of $454K. Contracting activity in FY2026 to date is down 36.3% year over year. Fiscal year history shows variation: obligations were $1.8B in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $1.9B in FY23, $2.9B in FY24, and $2.9B in FY25 before returning to $1.9B in FY26. The FY2026 to date totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and represent contract obligations rather than completed spending. This snapshot highlights concentration in a few large buyers and suppliers and a mix of manufacturing and services industries in the top NAICS categories.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contract spending in New Hampshire changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 36.3% year over year in FY2026 to date. Fiscal year comparisons show obligations of $2.9B in FY24 and $2.9B in FY25 before obligations returned to $1.9B in FY26. Award volume and average award size remained significant, with 4,091 awards and an average award size of $454K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate New Hampshire contracting in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B in FY2026 to date. BAE SYSTEMS INFORMATION AND ELECTRONIC SYSTEMS INTEGRATION INC. is the top vendor with $756M, followed by SIG SAUER INC. with $315M and ENVISION TECHNOLOGY, LLC with $69.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
